  Use:
    <manialink version="3"
               xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
               xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="manialink.xsd">

  The engine ignores XML namespaces. To validate a page that declares xmlns, remove it.

  Conventions:
    * An element or attribute is declared where the engine reads it. Names are case-sensitive.
    * The engine never rejects a bad value: it ignores it, or uses false, zero or a default.
      This schema reports such values as errors.
    * Case sensitivity of values follows the engine and differs per attribute.
    * Stray text in pages and frames is ignored by the engine, for example "//" comments, so it is
      accepted. In frame3d it is read as the image URL when no image is given.
    * "v<3", "v2+" and so on refer to <manialink version>. XSD 1.0 cannot enforce those
      conditions, so they are documented on the declarations.
    * Controls accept data-* attributes. XSD 1.0 cannot express that name pattern, so controls,
      frames, framemodel and frameinstance have an attribute wildcard. Consequence: on them, an
      attribute that is not declared for that element is not reported, and its value is not checked.
      That hides misspelled names, and also real attributes on the wrong element, for example
      <frame action="x"> or <playerlist size="garbage">. Declared attributes are still checked.

